WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.293 --> 00:00:17.036
The temple was high on a hill, and it was a clear day, so Brody could see far

2
00:00:17.096 --> 00:00:17.956
into the distance.

3
00:00:19.077 --> 00:00:21.197
And yet nothing he saw looked familiar.

4
00:00:22.758 --> 00:00:25.158
What had happened to the school and playing fields?

5
00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:29.279
Where were the houses and his favorite fast-food place?

6
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.420
"What's going on?"

7
00:00:31.804 --> 00:00:32.604
he blurted out.

8
00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:34.025
"Where are we?

9
00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:34.985
Where's the gym?"

10
00:00:35.005 --> 00:00:37.006
"The gymnasium?

11
00:00:37.386 --> 00:00:38.587
It's right over there, of course."

12
00:00:39.127 --> 00:00:40.488
Hermes pointed to the left.

13
00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.589
But Brody still didn't see anything that looked like the school gym.

14
00:00:44.609 --> 00:00:48.291
"It can't be," Julia murmured.

15
00:00:48.311 --> 00:00:51.532
"Are we really in ancient Olympia?"

16
00:00:51.552 --> 00:00:55.214
"What?" Brody said.

17
00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:57.795
"There's no way we traveled through time."

18
00:00:58.955 --> 00:01:00.896
Julia was staring at the city below.

19
00:01:02.344 --> 00:01:04.086
"What other explanation is there?"

20
00:01:05.226 --> 00:01:06.287
Brody rolled his eyes.

21
00:01:07.929 --> 00:01:12.512
People thought he was dumb, but he wasn't dumb enough to believe what Hermes and Caerus were saying.

22
00:01:13.553 --> 00:01:16.495
Only a freak like Julia would believe such a ridiculous story.

23
00:01:17.496 --> 00:01:18.137
Ancient Greece?

24
00:01:18.537 --> 00:01:19.098
Yeah, right!

25
00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:22.781
Still, there was definitely something weird going on.

26
00:01:23.861 --> 00:01:26.103
How could Brody make Hermes and Caerus admit it?

27
00:01:26.123 --> 00:01:28.165
"I've got it!"

28
00:01:28.485 --> 00:01:29.506
He pointed at Hermes.

29
00:01:29.526 --> 00:01:31.928
"You're lying, and I can prove it."

30
00:01:33.036 --> 00:01:34.516
Hermes raised one eyebrow.

31
00:01:34.536 --> 00:01:35.777
"Is that so?"

32
00:01:35.797 --> 00:01:41.698
"Yes. If we're in Greece, how come you guys are speaking English?"

33
00:01:42.639 --> 00:01:44.219
Brody was proud of himself.

34
00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:48.760
He might not be a genius, but he could figure things out when he needed to.

35
00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:53.762
"On the contrary, we're speaking proper Greek," Caerus said.

36
00:01:53.782 --> 00:01:57.983
"Hermes has powers over language and communication.

37
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:02.104
He has enabled you two to speak and understand Greek as if you were natives."

38
00:02:03.352 --> 00:02:04.272
Hermes smirked.

39
00:02:04.292 --> 00:02:06.353
"That's very important.

40
00:02:06.914 --> 00:02:10.315
After all, speaking Greek is a prerequisite for entering the Games."

41
00:02:11.796 --> 00:02:14.457
"Huh?" Brody didn't know what "prerequisite" meant.

42
00:02:15.917 --> 00:02:19.739
Before he could ask, Caerus glanced at Hermes and pantomimed eating.

43
00:02:19.759 --> 00:02:24.961
"Yes, this conversation is becoming dull," Hermes said to his friend.

44
00:02:25.981 --> 00:02:27.442
He turned to Brody and Julia.

45
00:02:27.462 --> 00:02:32.044
"If you're still confused, your mortal hosts can explain everything."

46
00:02:33.248 --> 00:02:35.709
"You'll be staying with the family that tends my temple."

47
00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.952
Caerus waved a hand to indicate the temple they had just exited.

48
00:02:39.972 --> 00:02:42.914
"Let's go," Hermes ordered.

49
00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.475
Brody was more confused than ever.

50
00:02:46.516 --> 00:02:48.937
And being confused made him mad.

51
00:02:48.957 --> 00:02:53.019
"I'm not going anywhere with you!"

52
00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.461
He gave Hermes a shove.

53
00:02:55.481 --> 00:02:57.262
"You're not gods.

54
00:02:57.562 --> 00:02:59.003
You're just jerks and fakers!"

55
00:03:00.603 --> 00:03:04.669
Suddenly a loud, chilling cry seemed to rip the air in two.

56
00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.591
At the same moment, Hermes transformed into an enormous hawk and dived at Brody.

57
00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.954
The hawk's giant talons stopped a hair's breadth from Brody's face.

58
00:03:24.974 --> 00:03:26.955
Brody fell back, gasping with fear.

59
00:03:27.775 --> 00:03:30.056
A second later Hermes looked normal again.

60
00:03:32.276 --> 00:03:33.696
"Learn this lesson well, mortal!"

61
00:03:34.157 --> 00:03:35.357
Hermes said sternly.

62
00:03:35.377 --> 00:03:38.098
"Do not defy me!

63
00:03:38.638 --> 00:03:40.759
I can be either your friend or your enemy.

64
00:03:41.559 --> 00:03:43.760
Trust me, you'd rather have me as a friend."

65
00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:47.821
"Come." Caerus headed down the steps of his temple.

66
00:03:47.841 --> 00:03:50.101
"Your hosts are waiting."

67
00:03:51.322 --> 00:03:55.603
Brody opened his mouth to argue again, but Hermes was still glaring at him.

68
00:03:55.623 --> 00:03:58.184
"Fine," Brody muttered.

69
00:03:59.752 --> 00:04:02.753
Caerus led the way to a modest home halfway down the hill.

70
00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:06.555
A bearded man wearing a purple robe stood in front.

71
00:04:06.575 --> 00:04:10.476
"Welcome, Caerus," the man said, bowing.

72
00:04:10.496 --> 00:04:13.118
"We are honored by your presence.

73
00:04:13.638 --> 00:04:14.958
Yours as well, Hermes."

74
00:04:14.978 --> 00:04:18.040
"Thank you," Hermes said.

75
00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:22.201
"Caerus tells me you've agreed to look after my champion until the Games."

76
00:04:22.221 --> 00:04:24.222
"Of course."

77
00:04:24.902 --> 00:04:26.223
The man bowed to Brody.

78
00:04:26.243 --> 00:04:29.128
"My name is Nikolaos.

79
00:04:29.148 --> 00:04:31.050
My eldest son will take care of your needs."

80
00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.472
A boy around Brody's age stepped outside.

81
00:04:35.513 --> 00:04:38.595
Like the men he wore one of those strange-looking chitons.

82
00:04:38.615 --> 00:04:41.077
"Hi," he said shyly.

83
00:04:41.097 --> 00:04:42.598
"I'm Markos."

84
00:04:42.618 --> 00:04:45.500
"Hey." Brody nodded.

85
00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:46.480
"I'm Brody."

86
00:04:47.321 --> 00:04:48.402
Julia stepped forward.

87
00:04:48.422 --> 00:04:49.523
"I'm Julia."

88
00:04:49.543 --> 00:04:52.665
"Oh, right," Caerus said.

89
00:04:52.685 --> 00:04:56.948
"We'll also need you to look after the champion's companion."

90
00:04:59.040 --> 00:04:59.600
"A girl?"

91
00:05:00.161 --> 00:05:02.702
Nikolaos stared at Julia, and then shrugged.

92
00:05:03.942 --> 00:05:05.002
"As you wish, Caerus.

93
00:05:05.383 --> 00:05:07.163
We can always use help in the kitchen."

94
00:05:08.324 --> 00:05:10.525
Julia frowned, but she didn't say anything.

95
00:05:11.825 --> 00:05:13.226
Soon the two gods left.

96
00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:19.088
"Take care of our guests, Markos," Nikolaos said.

97
00:05:19.108 --> 00:05:21.669
"I have important work to do at the temple."

98
00:05:21.689 --> 00:05:25.811
"Yes, Father," Markos said as Nikolaos left.

99
00:05:26.971 --> 00:05:28.752
Brody quickly glanced at Julia.

100
00:05:29.544 --> 00:05:30.664
"I'm going back to the temple.

101
00:05:31.044 --> 00:05:34.585
Caerus and Hermes said we could get home through that crack in the wall, so that's what I'm

102
00:05:34.626 --> 00:05:36.766
doing." "What?"

103
00:05:37.366 --> 00:05:38.607
Markos looked alarmed.

104
00:05:38.627 --> 00:05:40.607
"You can't leave!

105
00:05:41.027 --> 00:05:42.088
Hermes will be angry."

106
00:05:43.728 --> 00:05:44.548
Brody shrugged.

107
00:05:45.088 --> 00:05:45.569
"So what?"

108
00:05:46.849 --> 00:05:48.009
Markos shook his head.

109
00:05:48.029 --> 00:05:51.650
"Hermes may seem good-natured, but he is still a god.

110
00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:57.192
As you know, gods aren't like mortals, and they think nothing of punishing us at their whim."

111
00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:00.141
"How would I know that?"

112
00:06:00.641 --> 00:06:01.341
Brody said.

113
00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:05.383
"Up until a few minutes ago, I didn't know gods really existed."

114
00:06:06.543 --> 00:06:07.964
Markos looked confused.

115
00:06:07.984 --> 00:06:09.385
"What do you mean?"

116
00:06:09.405 --> 00:06:11.706
"Listen, Markos."

117
00:06:12.186 --> 00:06:13.066
Julia jumped in.

118
00:06:13.086 --> 00:06:17.508
"What's all this talk about Brody being Hermes' champion?

119
00:06:17.908 --> 00:06:20.369
And are the Olympic Games really starting soon?"

120
00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:22.930
Her questions tumbled out.

121
00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.251
"Is Hermes really a god?

122
00:06:25.512 --> 00:06:26.312
I mean, for real?"

123
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.581
Markos stared at her.

124
00:06:28.601 --> 00:06:31.503
"You ask many questions for a girl."

125
00:06:33.084 --> 00:06:34.205
Julia looked annoyed.

126
00:06:35.025 --> 00:06:39.088
Brody almost laughed, but he wanted to know the answer to her questions too.

127
00:06:39.108 --> 00:06:42.791
"Just answer her," he told Markos.

128
00:06:42.811 --> 00:06:47.614
"Yes, the Olympic Games begin soon," Markos said.

129
00:06:47.634 --> 00:06:54.018
"Every four years all the gods compete to see who can find the best mortal athlete."

130
00:06:55.619 --> 00:06:56.520
He shook his head.

131
00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.921
"But you must already know that."

132
00:06:58.941 --> 00:07:02.362
"No, we don't," Julia said.

133
00:07:02.382 --> 00:07:04.482
"We came from the future."

134
00:07:04.502 --> 00:07:06.383
"The future?

135
00:07:06.923 --> 00:07:07.863
I don't understand."

136
00:07:07.883 --> 00:07:12.464
"Wait Brody had just realized what Markos meant.

137
00:07:12.484 --> 00:07:17.366
"So Hermes thinks I'm the best athlete around?"

138
00:07:18.766 --> 00:07:19.687
Markos shrugged.

139
00:07:19.707 --> 00:07:21.287
"I suppose so."

140
00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:24.628
"And he wants me to be in the Olympics?"

141
00:07:25.188 --> 00:07:26.890
Brody liked the sound of that.

142
00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:31.535
"Cool!" But Julia was clearly worried.

143
00:07:31.555 --> 00:07:34.959
"We can't stay here," she told Brody.

144
00:07:34.979 --> 00:07:37.822
"We have to find a way home!"

145
00:07:37.842 --> 00:07:40.245
"Why the big rush?"

146
00:07:40.786 --> 00:07:41.567
Brody grinned.

147
00:07:41.587 --> 00:07:46.112
"If I get to be an Olympic champion, maybe I'll stick around!"
